  "steps": [
    "In a bowl, mix Greek yogurt/curd, water, red chilli powder, aamchur, black salt, jeera powder, chaat masala, and monkfruit extract. Stir well until fully combined. The consistency should be thinner than raita—adjust water if needed.",
    "Roast the makhana on medium flame until crispy. Immediately transfer to a bowl of boiling hot water and soak for 4-5 minutes until soft.",
    "Now, dip the softened makhana into the prepared yogurt mixture. Let it soak for at least 20-30 minutes so it absorbs all the flavors.",
    "Garnish with green chutney, imli chutney (limit to 1 tbsp for fewer cals), pomegranate seeds, extra chaat masala, and a pinch of red chilli powder.",
    "Serve chilled and enjoy this low-cal, high-protein chaat as a snack or meal!"
  ],
